{"type": "message", "id": "fd977633-ea2d-4038-84a3-98259f2e420a", "parentId": "7fc8d59d-8729-4fa7-9baa-25a6b47d30cd", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T06:26:21.635Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call3126da57886e4532a982d3d16ae541db", "toolName": "exec", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Convert an advisory-report Markdown file into a styled Word document.\n\nStyle (proven in source session conv_8487ad8077f4): A4, centered dark-blue H1,\ndark-blue H2/H3, light-blue table header shading, page header line + page\nnumber footer, CJK fonts (headings 黑体, body 宋体).\n\nNumbering discipline (session pitfall, msg 30/32): NO Word auto-numbering is\nused. Ordered list numbers stay as literal text authored in the Markdown, and\nbullets render as \"• \" text — this cannot collide with auto-numbering or\ngrow continuous 1-15 counters. Numbering rhythm (per-section restart) is the\nauthor's job in the Markdown.\n\nMarkdown subset: #/##/###/#### headings, paragraphs, **bold** spans, tables\n(| a | b | with --- separator), \"- \" bullets, \"N. \" ordered items, \"> \"\nblockquotes (indented gray), \"---\" rules skipped.\n\nUsage:\n  python md2docx.py 报告.md -o 报告.docx [--header 标题文本]\n\nExit codes: 0 ok, 2 usage/input error.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.enum.table import WD_TABLE_ALIGNMENT\nfrom docx.enum.text import WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH\nfrom docx.oxml import OxmlElement\nfrom docx.oxml.ns import qn\nfrom docx.shared import Cm, Pt, RGBColor\n\nDARK_BLUE = RGBColor(0x1F, 0x4E, 0x79)\nHEADER_BLUE_HEX = \"D9E2F3\"  # light blue table-header shading\nBODY_FONT = \"宋体\"\nHEADING_FONT = \"黑体\"\n\n\ndef _fail(msg):\n    print(\"md2docx error: \" + msg, file=sys.stderr)\n    return 2\n\n\ndef set_cjk(run, ascii_font, east_font, size, bold=False, color=None):\n    run.font.name = ascii_font\n    run.font.size = Pt(size)\n    run.font.bold = bold\n    if color is no